WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.663
Next, TLS.

2
00:00:01.663 --> 00:00:06.160
Learn's internet ingress design
guide says TLS one point two or one

3
00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.575
point three only, and on Application
Gateway, a predefined policy.

4
00:00:10.575 --> 00:00:14.125
The guide's command, from
Learn's Az PowerShell page,

5
00:00:14.125 --> 00:00:18.267
sets the predefined policy twenty
twenty-two oh one oh one S.

6
00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:23.169
Front Door Standard and Premium require
H T T P S on every custom domain,

7
00:00:23.169 --> 00:00:26.212
with custom certificates
kept in Key Vault.

8
00:00:26.212 --> 00:00:28.400
Then health probes and failover.

9
00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:33.223
Learn's Front Door quickstart builds an
origin group with probes and two origins in

10
00:00:33.223 --> 00:00:36.019
different regions, then
stops one origin to show

11
00:00:36.019 --> 00:00:39.025
the application stays
available through the other.

12
00:00:39.025 --> 00:00:41.475
The program exercises that twice a year.

13
00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:43.202
Cutting over is gentle too:

14
00:00:43.202 --> 00:00:47.992
run Front Door beside the old public
endpoint and compare logs before you

15
00:00:47.992 --> 00:00:52.625
change D N S, then close the origin's
public path one application at a time.

16
00:00:52.625 --> 00:00:57.260
Rollback removes the access
restriction and restores D N S.
